newscache (1.3.21-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging for Debian 13 (trixie) and Ubuntu 24.04: debhelper compat 13
    with the dh sequencer, autoreconf during the build, hardening flags
  * Build with PAM and ship /etc/pam.d/newscache
  * Ship a working /etc/newscache.conf that lets no client in
  * Depend on ca-certificates and netbase
  * systemd: add ExecReload; daily newscacheclean.timer replaces
    cron.daily; drop the SysV init script
  * Spool /var/cache/newscache owned by news, removed on purge
  * Machine-readable debian/copyright

 -- Billy G. <newscache-maintainer@pugleaf.net>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

newscache (1.3.21-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Shipped configs deny every client by default; allow clients with a
    Client entry (address or CIDR) or a login
  * IPv6 access-list entries are parsed as addresses on hosts without IPv6
  * A /prefix after a non-address is a config error
  * newscache -p and xdebug print access entries with their address
  * Dockerfile for Docker and Podman

 -- Billy G. <root@pugleaf.net>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:03:51 +0000

newscache (1.3.20-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * TLS: verify server certificates (chain, validity, host name), send SNI,
    use the system trust store; new TLSCAFile and Options noverify
  * STARTTLS: drop the connection if it is refused instead of continuing in
    plain text
  * Builds without GnuTLS refuse servers with ssl/starttls
  * newscache -p prints ssl, starttls and dontgenmsgid
  * Builds and checks out on macOS and Windows file systems
  * Sample config uses news.blueworldhosting.com; dead links replaced

 -- Billy G. <root@pugleaf.net>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 04:54:47 +0000

newscache (1.3.19-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix a crash at startup on hosts whose fully qualified domain name is
    64 characters or longer
  * README: NewsCache is developed at https://github.com/go-while/NewsCache

